-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party content included in this repository
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Ring Developer Playground footage
   Paths: fixtures/ring_playground/package/**, fixtures/ring_playground/vision_cache.json,
          fixtures/evidence/package.jpg, web/dashboard/public/ring/package.jpg,
          fixtures/playground/** (recorded API responses)

   Frames and API responses captured on 2026-10-11 from the Ring Developer
   Playground (simulated live view over WHEP, snapshots and REST responses)
   using a developer account. They are included only to let the
   demo and tests run without a live Playground token. The recorded REST
   responses belong to a Playground demo account ("Demo Developer",
   an example.com placeholder address); bearer tokens and pre-signed media tokens were
   never written to disk.

   The Playground "Package" scene (fixtures/ring_playground/package/**,
   fixtures/evidence/package.jpg, and web/dashboard/public/ring/package.jpg,
   a byte-identical copy of that evidence frame served by the hosted
   dashboard) is derived from:

     "Thief stealing our package"
     Author: YouTube user "frollard" (credit as shown by Ring under the clip
             in the Ring Developer Playground)
     Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
     (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
     Clipped from the original, as credited by Ring in the Developer
     Playground. DoorLedger further changed it: frames were re-encoded
     from the WHEP stream, sampled at about 1 frame per second, and
     saved as JPEG.

   The "Vehicle" and "Motion" (bird feeder) scenes carry no license
   statement in the Playground, so they are NOT included in this repository
   (capture them locally with scripts/capture_live.py and your own token).

2. YuNet face detection model
   Path: core/src/doorledger/models/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx
   Source: OpenCV Model Zoo,
           https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/face_detection_yunet
   License: MIT License. Copyright (c) the YuNet authors / OpenCV Model Zoo
   contributors. Used unmodified, only to pixelate faces in stored evidence
   frames.

3. Synthetic evaluation images
   Paths: eval/vision/images/**, eval/vision/contact_sheet.png
   Generated for this project with Stability AI "Stable Image Core" on Amazon
   Bedrock (2026-10-11), then post-processed (resize, barrel distortion, JPEG,
   PIL composites for phone screens and night-IR variants). They are subject
   to the Stability AI terms that applied when they were generated. They are
   synthetic: they show no real people or places.

4. Synthetic presence-code frames
   Paths: eval/presence/**
   Rendered by eval/presence/make_synthetic.py (part of this project).

5. QR Code encoder in the Caregiver Pass
   Path: web/caregiver-pass/index.html (block between "BEGIN DL-QR" and "END DL-QR")
   A compact port that follows the structure and formulas of the
   "QR Code generator library" by Project Nayuki
   (https://www.nayuki.io/page/qr-code-generator-library).
